# Month reconcile session (`/spending/reconcile`)

Dedicated triage page: stage **multiple** statement uploads for one month, auto-match against manuals, review queue, confirm once.

## Storage

`spending.reconcile_sessions["YYYY-MM"]` — `{ report_month, status, auto_match_ran, uploads[], excluded_manual_ids[], kept_manual_ids[], reviewed_unclaimed }`.

Each upload: `{ id, file_name, bank_source, period_start, period_end, rows[] }`. Row: `{ id, date, description, amount, direction, category, include, manual_match, transfer_pair, ledger_duplicate, reconcile_mark }`.

## Match kinds (`manual_match`)

- `single` — 1 bank row → 1 manual
- `netted_manuals` — 1 bank row → N manuals (exact sum)
- `netted_banks` — N bank rows → 1 manual (shared `group_key` on every leg)

## API routes

- `GET /spending/reconcile` — page
- `GET /api/spending/reconcile/<month>` — session payload (rows, manuals, totals, queue)
- `POST .../upload` — extract file → append upload. Form: `file`, optional `bank_source`, optional `period_start` / `period_end` (defaults to full month).
- `DELETE .../upload/<id>`
- `POST .../auto-match` — fuzzy + forward/reverse net + transfer pairs + exact bill auto-marks (`bill_auto_marks` in stats)
- `POST .../restart-match` — clear all session matches/triage, then auto-match again
- `POST .../link-manual`, `.../unlink-manual`, `.../link-transfer`, `.../unlink-transfer`, `.../relink-netted`
- `PATCH .../row/<id>` — `{ include, direction, reconcile_mark }` (`bill` or null)
- `POST .../mark-bills` — bulk `{ row_ids[], reconcile_mark: "bill"|null }` (Import search → mark visible / undo)
- `POST .../exclude-manual`, `.../keep-manual`, `.../review-unclaimed`
- `POST .../confirm` — requires `auto_match_ran`; if unclaimed manuals remain, requires `reviewed_unclaimed`

- Duplicate detection (`_reconcile_apply_duplicate_marks`) ignores fingerprints on **manual** txs. Claimed manuals copy the bank fingerprint; counting those as already-imported would zero `statement_count` after Find matches / a rematch.

## UI — effect-first cockpit (`@templates/reconcile.html`, `@static/reconcile.js`, `@static/style.css`)

Single scrolling screen (no wizard steps, no one-at-a-time carousel). Composer + staged uploads at the top, then one **grid** of every statement row plus a sticky **After import** panel. Classes are prefixed `rc-`.

- `.reconcile-page .hidden { display: none !important }` is required (panels use flex/grid and would otherwise beat Tailwind `.hidden`). The reconcile shell is widened: `.reconcile-page .app-shell { max-width: 1320px }`.
- Composer + **Adjust date range** (`#reconcile-range-toggle`, `#reconcile-period-start/end`) + staged uploads + **Find matches** (`#reconcile-auto-match-btn`) are unchanged from the pre-cockpit design.
- **Grid columns:** include checkbox · Bank row · Status · Matched entry · Amount · Actions (`#reconcile-rows`). Filters (`#reconcile-seg`): **To review** (asks + `NEW`, the default) / All / Matched / Bills / New / Transfers.
- **Status** (`kindOf`): quiet text labels for matched/bill/transfer/in; `NEW` is a solid blue pill; asks show `Near` or `N exact`. `NEW` rows are tinted blue; ask rows tinted amber.
- **Matched entry** shows the *logged entry being compared* (manual description + amount · date); bills show "Bill — not daily spending", transfers "↔ transfer". Clicking it opens an **inline resolver** (`data-resolve`): suggested candidates first (with `Np off`), then the full pool of `unclaimed` manuals, plus **Import as new** (`data-import-new`, client-only `state.decided`).
- **Row actions** (`rc-act`): **Unmatch** (`data-unmatch`) on matched rows; **Make bill** (`data-makebill`) on matched/new/ask. Unmatch/relink call `POST .../unlink-manual` / `.../link-manual`.
- **Reference grouping:** rows sharing the first two description tokens get a `×N` badge (`rc-ref-badge`). Clicking opens an inline group panel listing the affected dates/amounts with **Make all N bills** (`data-group-bill`, uses `POST .../mark-bills`) or Cancel. Badges are recomputed from current row kinds on every render.
- **Leftover** ("Logged, not on statements"): manuals with status `unclaimed`/`kept`/`excluded`; **Keep** / **Ignore** only (`POST .../keep-manual`, `.../exclude-manual`) — no Match (matching is driven from the bank-row side). Grid is `1fr auto` so the pills align in a right column.
- **After import panel** (`#reconcile-effect`, `#reconcile-daily`): Statement spend · Matched · New · Bills (with **Expected** from `expected_bills_total` and an under/over delta) · Transfers · Money in; then Logged entries · Unmatched · Ledger rows. Confirm CTA label counts *included* rows.
- **Undo toast** (`#reconcile-toast`, 7s): snapshot-free — the Undo handler replays the inverse calls (`mark-bills` null + `link-manual`, or `link-manual`). Covers Make bill / bulk Make bills / Unmatch.
- **Confirm** (`POST .../review-unclaimed` then `.../confirm`) — the review-unclaimed POST satisfies the server guard when unclaimed manuals remain.
- `status == imported` is read-only: composer + cockpit hidden, `#reconcile-readonly` summary shown (files · statement rows · outgoing · matched · bills · new).
- `bank_matched_via`: `reconcile_auto` | `reconcile_user`. Excluded manuals get `reconcile_excluded_month` on confirm.

## Backend invariants (bill flag + payment ref)

- **`is_bill`** is persisted on imported statement txs that were marked as bills (`_reconcile_confirm_session`). `_daily_budget_is_discretionary_tx` excludes `is_bill` (and bill/ignore categories). This is the durable bill signal — the category stays *truthful*.
- `_reconcile_bill_import_category` prefers the row's own valid category, else the matching Daily → Plan bill item's category, else `'other'` (no more `'utilities'` fallback).
- `_daily_budget_estimate_bills_for_month` also treats `is_bill` merchant slots as bill candidates (so explicitly-marked bills still surface when re-estimating the Plan).
- **Matched payment ref:** on claim, the ledger description becomes **bank ref · manual ref** via `_merge_payment_refs` (bank-only when the manual title is empty/generic). The write-only `bank_description` field was removed.

